{"availability":"available","full":"moq-dev/moq","name":"moq","description":"Media over QUIC: Real-time latency at massive scale","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":1569,"forks":261,"created":"2022-06-29T16:16:37Z","updated":"2026-10-16T20:31:38Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://moq.dev","topics":["live","media","moq","quic","real-time"],"demo":"https://doc.moq.dev/setup/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T20:32:18.009Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T20:32:18.009Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T20:32:18.009Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:34.719Z","stars":1555,"forks":252},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:42:44.846Z","stars":1557,"forks":252},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:02:49.181Z","stars":1557,"forks":254},{"at":"2026-10-10T23:18:45.537Z","stars":1561,"forks":257},{"at":"2026-10-16T20:32:18.009Z","stars":1569,"forks":261}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Media over QUIC (MoQ) is a next-generation live media protocol that provides real-time latency at massive scale. Built using modern web technologies, MoQ delivers WebRTC-like latency without the constraints of WebRTC. The core networking is delegated to a QUIC library but the rest is in application-space, giving you full control over your media pipeline.","Note: This project implements moq-lite, a forwards-compatible subset of the IETF moq-transport draft. moq-lite works with any moq-transport CDN (ex. Cloudflare). The focus is narrower, prioritizing simplicity and deployability."],"features":["🚀 Real-time latency using QUIC for prioritization and partial reliability.","📈 Massive scale designed for fan-out and supports cross-region clustering.","🌐 Modern Web using WebTransport, WebCodecs, and WebAudio.","🎯 Multi-language with both Rust (native) and TypeScript (web) libraries.","🔧 Generic for any live data, not just media. Includes text chat as both an example and a core feature."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/moq-dev/